  "configuration_id": "config_033",
  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_039: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted; acc=0.725) shows that adding image to multi-profile RNA yields a substantial gain (~0.65→0.72). However, we have only tested one image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) in the multimodal setting. Image-only experiments show a small but present encoder effect (resnet50=0.208 vs imagenet_vit_l=0.227). Config_033 changes only the image encoder (imagenet_vit_l→resnet50) while keeping all other settings identical to config_039, cleanly isolating whether image encoder quality matters when the image is a secondary modality. If performance is similar, the image contributes a complementary signal regardless of encoder sophistication, and we can redirect budget to other variables (e.g., aggregation or RNA encoder in the multimodal context). If resnet50 degrades notably, it confirms the image encoder is a bottleneck and justifies prioritizing the stronger encoder. This single-variable comparison is the most efficient way to reduce uncertainty about the image modality's contribution mechanism under the limited budget."
}

